stinguishable from the desired procedure. No idea yet how to address this, maybe a more explicit code....","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1495020130,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMwMjA2MTAzMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1419#issuecomment-302061032"},"message":"@yarikoptic OK, I am on this now. The issue is bigger than it seemed. Not only undesired adding of content in subdatasets, but in general. We even have a test for that :(\n\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/master/datalad/distribution/tests/test_create.py#L160\n\nIn this test we check whether `ds.save(recursive=True, all_updated=True)` yields a clean top-level repo -- and it does -- but each dataset (incl. the top) has untracked files, which are all added at the end -- shouldn't be.\n\nI have a draft of a new `save` implementation that doesn't do that anymore.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1495193863,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEwODkzODE3ODY="},"added":["fix-implemented"],"removed":[]},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1496839692,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTExMzU4MjkxNA=="},"status":2}]}